From 09362181f99b871ff7709d1c14335afe684a5578 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joss Gray <joss@jossgray.net>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 16:22:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] tests/fate: add NotchLC decoder tests

NotchLC had no coverage at all. Add five framemd5 tests covering the alpha
block types, the chroma ramp paths and non-multiple-of-16 dimensions.

alpha-ramp, alpha-ramp-oddsize and chroma-alpha fail against the decoder
as it stood before the recent alpha fixes. alpha-blocks and
alpha-macroblocks exercise only the opaque and transparent block types and
are plain regression guards.

The tests use framemd5 rather than framecrc because alpha-blocks.mov and
alpha-macroblocks.mov both produce framecrc 0xd37626e8 despite their
different spatial arrangements, while their MD5s differ. A framecrc
reference would therefore not tell the two patterns apart.

The samples are synthetic patterns encoded with the NotchLC Adobe CC
plugin and still need uploading to fate-suite under notchlc/.

The Forgejo Fairy review of PR #23791 found that native byte order makes
all five NotchLC test references fail on big-endian hosts.

Select yuva444p12le and use an explicit scale filter because FATE disables
automatic conversion. Require SCALE_FILTER when selecting these tests.

All five tests pass on AArch64 with the existing references. They are
excluded when SCALE_FILTER is disabled.

Assisted-by: Fairy
